msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Help.php:120
msgid "Add a service"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Help.php:121
msgid "Register a service on the `silvertrail_register` action, in a plugin or the theme."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Help.php:124
msgid "`group`: `essential`, `preferences`, `statistics`, `marketing` or `external-media`. `silvertrail_register_group()` adds your own."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Help.php:125
msgid "`hosts`: embeds from these hosts wait behind a placeholder."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Help.php:126
msgid "`handles`: scripts enqueued under these handles wait for consent."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Help.php:127
msgid "Keep the config the same on every request. Every visitor is asked again when the set of services changes."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Help.php:131
msgid "Change a service"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Help.php:132
msgid "Register a service again by its ID, with only the fields to change."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Help.php:135
msgid "A preset’s ID turns the preset on with its defaults. A tracker needs only its `tag_id`."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Help.php:136
msgid "The `silvertrail_config` filter runs last. It edits or removes any service, even one turned on here."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Help.php:137
msgid "The Services tab marks each preset that code turned on, changed or removed."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Help.php:141
msgid "Gate a script"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Help.php:142
msgid "Give the script the type `text/plain` and the service ID. The browser runs it once the visitor agrees."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Help.php:145
msgid "Inline and external scripts keep their order."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Help.php:146
msgid "A script that WordPress enqueues needs no change: list its handle under the service’s `handles`."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Help.php:150
msgid "Settings in code"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Help.php:151
msgid "The `silvertrail_settings` filter sets any setting. A field set in code shows “Set in code” on this page and cannot be changed here."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Help.php:154
msgid "On this page: `enabled`, `layout`, `appearance`, `require_choice`, `imprint_page`, `records`."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Help.php:155
msgid "Only in code: `floating_button` (`auto`, `always` or `never`), `load_css`, `expiry_months`, `retention_days`, `gpc`, `trail`."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Help.php:156
msgid "`wp silvertrail settings` lists each value and where it comes from."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Help.php:160
#: includes/Admin/tabs/banner.php:251
msgid "Texts"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Help.php:161
msgid "Ship the texts with the theme as `silvertrail/texts-{locale}.json`, or `silvertrail/texts.json` for every language. The Banner tab shows the JSON with every key."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Help.php:164
msgid "A child theme wins over its parent."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Help.php:165
msgid "From a plugin, return another path or an array in the `silvertrail_translation` filter."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Help.php:166
msgid "Edits on the Banner tab win over the file. The `silvertrail_texts` filter runs last."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Help.php:167
msgid "`wp silvertrail validate` reports unknown keys and broken files."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Help.php:171
#: includes/Admin/tabs/banner.php:108
msgid "Design"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Help.php:172
msgid "The banner takes its colors, corners and buttons from the theme’s `theme.json`. The `silvertrail_design` filter changes them."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Help.php:175
msgid "Keys: `background`, `text`, `muted`, `line`, `accent`, `on-accent`, `radius`, `button-padding`, `button-weight`. Each becomes a `--silvertrail-<key>` custom property."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Help.php:176
msgid "For anything else, add `silvertrail/silvertrail.css` to the theme. It loads after the default styles."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Help.php:177
msgid "`styling.md` in the plugin folder is a brief for an AI assistant that writes this stylesheet."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Help.php:178
msgid "To change the markup, copy a file from `templates/` into the theme’s `silvertrail/` folder and keep the `data-silvertrail-*` attributes."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Help.php:182
msgid "Links to the preferences"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Help.php:183
msgid "Any link to `#silvertrail` opens the preferences, and so does any element with `data-silvertrail-open`."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Help.php:186
msgid "The `[silvertrail_link]` shortcode and the Privacy settings link block print such a link."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Help.php:187
msgid "The floating button steps aside on pages that have one. `floating_button` in the `silvertrail_settings` filter sets it to `always` or `never`."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Help.php:191
msgid "JavaScript"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Help.php:192
msgid "`window.silvertrail` reads and changes the choice in the browser."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Help.php:195
msgid "`has( id )`: whether the visitor agreed to the service. Essential services are always `true`."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Help.php:196
msgid "`open()`: opens the preferences."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Help.php:197
msgid "`silvertrail:change`: fires on `window` after every choice."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Help.php:198
msgid "`silvertrail:before-prompt`: answer `prompt`, `accept-all` or `reject-all` within three seconds, for example by region."
msgstr ""

